  \item \textbf{Enterprise Order Management Systems (e.g., Cin7, Large Enterprise OMS):} Priced at \$350 to \$1,000+ per month, these platforms support real-time sync, duplicate handling, and full audit trails, and allow priority allocation rules. However, their rules are \textit{static}—configured once by an administrator and never self-improving—and their subscription cost prices out small and mid-scale multi-channel sellers.
  \item \textbf{Standalone Profit \& Analytics Tools (e.g., TrueProfit):} Priced at \$50 to \$300/month as a separate add-on subscription, these tools compute order-level profit and customer behavior metrics, but have zero connection to real-time inventory synchronization or conflict resolution.
