\section{Risk Management w.r.t. NP Hard analysis}
In general multi-warehouse, multi-SKU bundle fulfillment with time-varying channel SLA penalties and non-linear shipping constraints, finding the globally optimal subset of orders to fulfill vs. unwind over a rolling horizon reduces to the \textbf{0--1 Multidimensional Knapsack Problem}, which is known to be \textbf{NP-Hard}. Waiting for an exact exponential-time solver during a live webhook storm would violate real-time latency requirements. To mitigate this computational risk, our Python conflict engine employs a fast $O(k \log k)$ multi-criteria priority scoring heuristic over the active contention window $\mathcal{W}(s, \Delta t)$, achieving near-optimal margin retention in sub-millisecond execution time.

\subsection{Risk Identification}
Following Pressman's risk identification framework \cite{bookPressman}, the project scope, requirements, and distributed architecture were evaluated against standard software engineering risk questionnaires:
