\subsection{Activity Diagram}
The end-to-end activity workflow follows six deterministic steps:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Step 1:} Channel emits sale/return/restock webhook to Nginx load balancer.
  \item \textbf{Step 2:} Assigned Node.js intake node executes atomic Redis \texttt{SETNX} check on \texttt{event\_id}; if duplicate, returns HTTP 200 immediately and halts.
  \item \textbf{Step 3:} If new, intake node publishes event to durable RabbitMQ queue and acknowledges webhook.
  \item \textbf{Step 4:} Python worker consumes event, appends it to PostgreSQL \texttt{inventory\_events}, and folds current stock $Q_t$.
  \item \textbf{Step 5:} If $Q_t < 0$, worker compares contending orders by profit margin and customer importance, unwinds the lower-priority order via a compensating event, notifies the customer, and logs the full explanation.
  \item \textbf{Step 6:} Dashboard updates live stock, order profit, and—if conflict threshold is reached—surfaces a human-reviewable buffer suggestion.
\end{itemize}

