\chapter{Conclusion and future scope}

\section*{Conclusion}
The \textbf{Multi-Channel Inventory Reconciliation Engine} addresses a critical, costly operational gap faced by small and mid-scale multi-channel sellers operating across platforms like Amazon, Flipkart, direct websites, and physical POS counters. By replacing periodic polling and destructive stock overwrites with an immutable \textbf{Event Sourcing} ledger in PostgreSQL, horizontally scaled Node.js + Express webhook intake nodes behind Nginx, sub-millisecond Redis duplicate filtering, durable RabbitMQ queuing, and Python-based priority conflict resolution, the system guarantees that no sale event is lost, no duplicate notification is counted twice, and simultaneous last-unit race conditions are resolved intelligently based on profit margin and customer value. Most importantly, by introducing a \textbf{self-improving, human-approved recommendation loop} that watches its own conflict history and proposes targeted buffer adjustments while keeping a human in final control of every financial decision, our system delivers enterprise-grade reliability and built-in profit intelligence in one unified, affordable package.

\section*{Future Scope}
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Multi-Warehouse Geo-Distributed Routing:} Extending the priority conflict resolver to factor in warehouse-to-customer shipping distance and split-shipment costs across regional fulfillment centers.
  \item \textbf{Seasonal Demand Spike Forecasting:} Combining the historical conflict ledger with festival/flash-sale calendar signals (e.g., Diwali / Big Billion Days / Great Indian Festival) to suggest pre-event safety buffers ahead of traffic surges.
  \item \textbf{Plug-and-Play Marketplace Connectors:} Expanding native OAuth webhook adapters for Shopify, WooCommerce, ONDC (Open Network for Digital Commerce), and quick-commerce platforms.
\end{itemize}

